name Quantification of Enhancement and Failure Thresholds
msg
Quantification of Enhancement and Failure Thresholds
Authored by Senior Artificer Ilvane Marr. Marginal calculations preserved.
This document concerns the measurable limits of artificial alteration and the probability of failure as alteration intensity increases.

1. Enhancement Levels

Alterations occur in discrete levels rather than a smooth continuum. Early levels produce modest improvements with low risk. Later levels produce disproportionately larger improvements accompanied by sharply increased failure rates.
This relationship is non-linear. Attempting higher-level alterations prematurely is statistically unsound.

2. Attempt Difficulty
Each operation carries an inherent difficulty influenced by:
The current enhancement level of the target.
The compatibility between target and inorganic material.
The quality and freshness of components.
Difficulty increases after every successful alteration of the same target.
Observational note: Two identical items altered independently do not necessarily share the same difficulty curve after initial enhancement.

3. Failure Modes
Failures fall into three categories:
Neutral failure: materials consumed, no change to target.
Degradative failure: target loses effectiveness.
Aberrant success: target is altered in an unintended manner.
Aberrant outcomes are rare but not random. They occur most often when attempting high-level alterations using marginal materials.

4. Indicators of Excessive Risk
Terminate the procedure immediately if any of the following are observed prior to catalyst introduction:
Spontaneous heating of materials.
Movement within the container without external influence.
Darkening or coagulation of the catalyst.
Proceeding under these conditions resulted in catastrophic loss in 82% of recorded cases.

5. Practical Recommendations
Incremental improvement yields better long-term results than aggressive enhancement. Materials should be matched carefully to the intended alteration rather than chosen for rarity alone.

No recorded artificer achieved consistent success beyond the upper enhancement levels without extensive material loss.
endmsg
